        "text_sha256": "f5b0b21a363d4e4192b3b9c6db1ca1c4041e1f77c2b8b7e5973e1a8f70097afa",
        "excerpt": "EA_Hydroacoustics Data - Marine Geoscience Data System\nAbout\nMGDS Overview\nNews\nSystem Citations\nStatistics & Holdings\nContact Us\nTerms of Use\nTools\nContribute Data\nSearch for Data\nGoogle Earth KMLs\nMarine-Geo Explorer\nReference Search\nWeb Services\nData Collections\nAcademic Seismic Portal\nAntarctic & Southern Ocean\nGeoPRISMS\nMARGINS\nRidge 2000\nLong Island Sound\nResources\nData Publication\nData Management Plan\nHelp & Tutorials\nRelated Links\nSearch Data »\nEA_Hydroacoustics\nEarthquake:Catalog:Microseismicity, Seismic:Passive\nMap View\nT-phase location catalog for equatorial Atlantic ocean, 2011-2015\nCatalog of T-phase origins from August 2011 to January 2015, located using waveform arrivals recorded by an array of 8 autonomous moored hydrophones and the hydroacoustic station HA10 (Ascension) maintained by the Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty Organization. Instruments were placed in the Sound Fixing And Ranging (SOFAR) channel. Event locations are expected to be associated with earthquakes on transform faults and spreading segments along the equatorial Mid-Atlantic Ridge. The data file is in ASCII text format and contains a header line that describes the file content. The data set was generated as part of the projects called Seismicity of the Equatorial Mid-Atlantic Ridge and Its Large Offset Transforms; and, Along-Axis Continuity of Oceanic Detachment Faults. Funded was provided by NSF awards NSF EAR-1062238, EAR-1062165, and OCE-1839727.\nParnell-Turner, Ross\nInvestigator\nSIO\nDziak, Robert\nInvestigator\nNOAA\nSmith, Deborah\nInvestigator\nNSF:OCE\nDevice Info\nHydrophone\nPlatform\nNotApplicable\nAwards\nEAR10-62165\nEAR10-62238\nOCE18-39727\nData DOI\n10.26022/IEDA/330497\nQuality\n2\nThe data have been processed/modified to a level beyond that of basic quality control (e.g. final processed sonar data, photo-mosaics).\nLicense\nCC BY-NC-SA 3.0\nReport Incorrect Information\nSelect All\nRequest Selected File(s)\nDownload Selected File(s)\nData Files\nReferences\nAcquisition Information\nData Citation Information\nISO/XML Metadata\nReferences\nParnell-Turner et al., 2022\nHydroacoustic Monitoring of Seafloor Spreading and Transform Faulting in the Equatorial Atlantic Ocean\nJGR Solid Earth\n. doi:\n10.1029/2022JB024008\nDownload Data Set Metadata Report\nXML\nDownload\nMGDS formatted data set xml report containing verbose file and data set level metadata\nISO XML\nDownload\nISO 19115-compliant xml report containing general data set level metadata\nRelated Acquisition Information\nEA_Hydroacoustics\nStation:WaterColumn Log\nHow To Cite This Data\nExpand\nHosted at\nLamont-Doherty Earth Observatory\nof\nColumbia University\n.\nSite licensed under\nCreative Commons Attribution-Noncommercial-Share Alike 3.0\nAcknowledgments\n|\nPrivacy\n|\nContact\nFunded by the\nUS National Science Foundation (NSF)",
